From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 10:20:48 -0400
Subject: spaces: isolate cookies per Space in a storage partition

An optional Independent session on a Space puts its tabs in a
non-default StoragePartition so the same site can be signed into
twice in one window. Off, Spaces share the profile jar. Essentials
stay shared. Moving a tab rebinds it; restore keeps the jar.
Menu, Settings, and the command bar all expose the toggle.

Why: docs/features/sessions.md S1-S12, ADR 0019.
Removable when: Chromium offers per-tab storage partitions as a
product feature, or Spaces become full Profiles.
